Doug Freyburger wrote:

> I think pets know the strength of unarmed monsters but don't
> make guesses as to the damage done by that monster's
> weapons.

Strength isn't quite right. Inspecting the source at
    http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Dogmove.c#dog_move
starting at line 616, I deduced the following.

If any of the following are true, the pet will not attack the monster.

* the enemy XL is at least 2 levels higher than the pet

* 90% of the time when the enemy is a floating eye and can be seen by
the pet

* 90% of the time when the enemy is a gelatinous cube (9/10)

* the "max passive damage" done by the enemy is greater than the pet's
current HP

* the enemy is a stoning monster and the pet is not stoning-resistant

* if the enemy is peaceful and there is no conflict on, and either
** the pet's current HP is less than 1/4 of the enemy' max HP
** or the enemy is MS_GUARDIAN (a guardian angel, I think)
** or the enemy is MS_LEADER (the quest leader, I think)

So if it gets past ALL of those tests, then the pet will attack.

"max passive damage" is "the maximum damage a defender can do to the
attacker via a passive defense".  Passive damages are suffered when you
attack an acid monster, or an exploding monster, or cold, fire,
electricity, or "physical".  I don't think this takes into account how
much the monster could do in pummeling during its own turn; I think
it's only the passive damage taken when the pet attacks.



